"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Resumed claimed ticket; beginning held-out TDD in worktree janitor-828b-fe4a.","timestamp":1788468511986489840},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"SCOPE CORRECTION (orchestrator, 2026-09-03): the leaf agent correctly identified that the\ndeclared file_impact omitted the LIBRARY surface of the boolean-force deprecation. The three\nscheduled deprecations (see src/rebar/_deprecations.py:101-112) are (1) rebar.transition(force_close=...),\n(2) rebar.transition(force=True) — both public LIBRARY surfaces in src/rebar/_lib_writes.py\n(_normalize_transition_force + transition signature/doc) — and (3) the hosted openai-chat provider\nprefix. Added src/rebar/_lib_writes.py to file_impact so the library-boundary ACs can be\nsatisfied. This is a file_impact correction, not a scope expansion; the ticket already claimed,\nso the prior plan-review PASS is not re-gated. No other Wave-1 agent touches _lib_writes.py.","timestamp":1788468751020979937},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"SCOPE CORRECTION #2 (orchestrator): the hosted-openai-chat deprecation removal also requires the\nresolution cluster — src/rebar/llm/model_classes.py (_resolve_target) and\nsrc/rebar/llm/anthropic_model.py (_pai_model), which currently honor/preserve hosted openai-chat.\nAdded both to file_impact. NUANCE (per _deprecations.py:105-112 and the code comments): ONLY the\nHOSTED-OpenAI openai-chat prefix/provider (no custom base_url) is the scheduled deprecation ->\nreplacement openai-responses. An EXPLICIT openai-chat with a CUSTOM base_url/endpoint (a custom\nOpenAI-compatible server whose /v1/responses support is unknown) is a SUPPORTED selection and must\nbe PRESERVED. The oracle must encode this hosted-vs-custom distinction. No other Wave-1 agent\ntouches llm/*.","timestamp":1788469095405204402}],"created_at":1788314214336944001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`src/rebar/_deprecations.py:94-112` schedules three public removals: the Python-library `rebar.transition(force_close=...)` keyword, boolean `rebar.transition(force=True)`, and explicit hosted-OpenAI `openai-chat:` model selection. Closed migration `blusterous-earthly-kitten` established the temporary warning mappings; this ticket is the scheduled retirement, not a duplicate. These registry-adjacent removals are intentionally one pre-1.0 release increment: one compatibility deadline, one breaking-change notice, and separate subsystem-specific test coverage.\n\n## End State\n\nThe Python library accepts only a reason-bearing string `force=\"<reason>\"`. `force_close` or boolean `force=True` fail at the library boundary with `force=\"<reason>\"` named as the replacement. Hosted model selection accepts `openai-responses:<model>`. Both live hosted-resolution paths reject explicit `openai-chat:`. Custom OpenAI-compatible `base_url` selection retains its Chat Completions dialect.\n\n## Implementation Plan\n\n1. Retire library mappings in `_lib_writes` plus `_deprecations`. Do not add an environment or configuration tombstone: these are callable inputs, so validation belongs at the Python boundary.\n2. Regenerate the API snapshot plus MCP-library parity manifest after the library signature changes.\n3. Retire hosted explicit `openai-chat:` in `_resolve_target` plus `_pai_model`/`_openai_wire_prefix`. Preserve custom-endpoint routing. Migrate hosted `gpt-5.4*` inventory to `openai-responses:`.\n4. Retarget each test that currently preserves hosted `openai-chat:` to a hosted rejection assertion. Retain each custom-endpoint Chat assertion.\n5. Regenerate `docs/config-reference.md` via `scripts/gen_config_reference.py`. Migrate all maintained hosted examples plus workflow-schema descriptions to `openai-responses:`.\n6. Replace the two legacy warn-and-map tests in `test_force_unification_blusterous.py` with rejection tests. Retarget each behavior-preserving caller in `test_completion_gate.py`, `test_ac_checkbox_precheck_heldout.py`, `test_attestations_integration.py`, `test_plan_review_close_gate_lifecycle.py`, `test_attested_close_guard_e2e.py`, and `test_transition_open_children.py` to `force=\"<reason>\"`.\n7. Update maintained release/API guidance. Preserve historical `force_close_reason` durable state.\n\n## File Impact\n\n- `src/rebar/_deprecations.py`, `src/rebar/_lib_writes.py` — retired library inputs\n- `tests/unit/api_surface_baseline.json`, `scripts/gen_api_surface.py` — generated public signature snapshot\n- `tests/unit/mcp_library_parity_manifest.json`, `scripts/check_mcp_library_parity.py` — retired library-only parity divergence\n- `src/rebar/llm/runner.py`, `src/rebar/llm/model_classes.py`, `src/rebar/llm/anthropic_model.py`, `src/rebar/llm/config.py`, `.github/llm-providers/openai.toml` — hosted resolution plus deployed model inventory\n- `tests/unit/test_openai_responses_migration.py`, `test_pydantic_ai_runner.py`, `test_llm_capabilities.py`, `test_model_classes.py`, `test_openai_compatible_provider.py`, `test_provider_qualifier.py`, `tests/interfaces/store/test_llm_framework.py` — hosted rejection plus custom-endpoint preservation\n- `docs/config-reference.md`, `scripts/gen_config_reference.py`, `tests/unit/test_gen_config_reference.py` — cfg-kind output\n- `docs/llm-example-configs.md`, `docs/workflow-authoring-v2.md`, `docs/llm-framework.md`, `src/rebar/schemas/workflow.v1.schema.json`, `workflow.v2.schema.json`, `workflow.v3.schema.json` — maintained hosted examples\n- `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_force_unification_blusterous.py`, `test_completion_gate.py`, `test_ac_checkbox_precheck_heldout.py`, `test_attestations_integration.py`, `test_plan_review_close_gate_lifecycle.py`, `test_attested_close_guard_e2e.py`, `test_transition_open_children.py` — rejection migration plus canonical callers\n- `CHANGELOG.md`, `docs/release-notes.md` — breaking-release guidance\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `rebar.transition(force_close=\"legacy\")` is rejected at the Python-library boundary. Its error names `force=\"<explicit reason>\"`.\n- [ ] `rebar.transition(force=True)` is rejected at the Python-library boundary. Its error names `force=\"<explicit reason>\"`.\n- [ ] `rebar.transition(force=\"approved reason\")` remains accepted.\n- [ ] `tests/unit/api_surface_baseline.json` is regenerated through `scripts/gen_api_surface.py`. Its `transition` signature has no `force_close` row.\n- [ ] `tests/unit/mcp_library_parity_manifest.json` removes the retired `force_close` divergence.\n- [ ] `tests/unit/mcp_library_parity_manifest.json` removes the retired `force_close` `library_params` entry.\n- [ ] `scripts/check_mcp_library_parity.py` passes.\n- [ ] The CLI retains its existing retired-input rejection. This ticket adds no CLI force-close removal.\n- [ ] The MCP transition schema remains free of `force_close`. This ticket adds no MCP force-close removal.\n- [ ] Hosted `openai-chat:gpt-4o` is rejected through `_resolve_target`.\n- [ ] Hosted `openai-chat:gpt-4o` is rejected through `_pai_model`.\n- [ ] Hosted `openai-responses:gpt-4o` succeeds.\n- [ ] A custom endpoint retains Chat Completions routing.\n- [ ] Every listed resolver test distinguishes the rejected hosted case from the preserved custom-endpoint case.\n- [ ] Each hosted `gpt-5.4*` entry in `.github/llm-providers/openai.toml` uses `openai-responses:`.\n- [ ] `scripts/gen_config_reference.py --check` passes with the retired hosted cfg row absent.\n- [ ] Each listed maintained document plus workflow schema replaces hosted `openai-chat:gpt-4o` with its Responses equivalent.\n- [ ] `test_force_unification_blusterous.py` has no warning-plus-mapping assertion for `force_close` or boolean `force`.\n- [ ] Every listed behavior-preserving lifecycle caller uses canonical `force=\"<reason>\"`.\n- [ ] `rg -n -U \"rebar\\.transition\\([\\s\\S]{0,500}?(force_close\\s*=|force\\s*=\\s*True)\" tests` has expected matches only in explicit retired-input rejection tests.\n- [ ] Maintained release/API documentation names the replacements. Historical durable `force_close_reason` state remains intact.\n- [ ] Focused boundary checks pass.\n- [ ] Focused resolver checks pass.\n- [ ] Focused provider checks pass.\n- [ ] Generated-reference checks pass.\n- [ ] Lint passes.\n- [ ] Typecheck passes.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_deprecations.py","reason":"remove scheduled deprecation registry entries"},{"path":"src/rebar/_lib_writes.py","reason":"remove public rebar.transition(force_close=..., force=True) boolean-force compat (library surface)"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/transition.py","reason":"remove force_close/boolean-force compatibility paths (CLI surface)"},{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py","reason":"update public MCP transition contract (MCP surface)"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/providers.py","reason":"remove hosted openai-chat compatibility selection"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/model_classes.py","reason":"_resolve_target hosted openai-chat resolution/preservation (part of the hosted openai-chat deprecation)"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/anthropic_model.py","reason":"_pai_model hosted openai-chat resolution/preservation (part of the hosted openai-chat deprecation)"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/runner.py","reason":"remove hosted openai-chat deprecation warning + fallback resolution (runner.py:366 warn_deprecated for hosted openai-chat: with no base_url)"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/config.py","reason":"migrate hosted openai-chat:gpt